[29.079528, "o", "\r\u001b[K`git log -p` shows the commit history **with patches**.\r\n\r\n- `git log` lists commits (hash, author, date, message).\r\n- `-p` / `--patch` adds the diff introduced by each commit: changed files plus added (`+`) and removed (`-`) lines.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```bash\r\ngit log -p\r\n```\r\n\r\nUseful variants:\r\n```bash\r\ngit log -p -n 3       # patches for the latest 3 commits\r\ngit log -p -- file.py # patches affecting only file.py\r\ngit log -p HEAD~2..HEAD  # patches in a commit range\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt displays committed changes, not uncommitted working-tree edits; use `git diff` for those.\r\n"]
